{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"answers\":[{\"question_id\":\"Q016_pdb_1acc_domain_split\",\"answer\":\"SCOP 1.75 represented the classified portion of PDB 1acc chain A as one domain, d1acca_ (A:, SUNID 43828), assigned to f.11.1.1: the Anthrax protective antigen family and superfamily, Anthrax protective antigen fold, in class f (membrane and cell-surface proteins and peptides). SCOPe 2.01–2.03 retained that definition. Beginning with SCOPe 2.04, it was replaced by two nonoverlapping domains, a split retained through the current release 2.08: d1acca2 is the N-terminal A:14-225 segment (SUNID 238522; b.179.1.1), classified in the PA14 family, PA14-like superfamily, Anthrax protective antigen N-terminal-like fold, and all-beta class; d1acca1 is the C-terminal A:226-735 segment (SUNID 238521; f.60.1.1), classified in the Anthrax protective antigen C-terminal-like family, superfamily, and fold within class f. Thus the former f.11 classification was not simply renamed: one whole-chain domain was repartitioned into two modules with distinct folds and even different structural classes.\\n\\nThe revision illustrates that a domain is an inferred evolutionary module rather than merely an entire chain or an immutable geometric partition. The two regions occur in one protective-antigen chain but have separable evolutionary histories; their linkage does not make them homologous to each other. Family membership supports relatively close homology, superfamily membership supports probable common ancestry at greater divergence, whereas fold membership alone is structural evidence and does not establish homology. A hit to either new domain therefore cannot safely transfer the other domain, the complete chain architecture, or full protective-antigen/toxin function.\\n\\nHomology searches should use the two residue ranges separately (or domain-specific profiles), evaluate coverage and significance per module, and then examine whether the target has the same domain architecture and order. A full-chain query can let one module dominate, miss shorter or rearranged homologs, or encourage annotation transfer across an unrelated segment. Templates likewise should be selected for the matching domain; whole-chain modeling additionally requires evidence for compatible architecture and interdomain geometry. Release-specific representative sets must not treat old d1acca_ and its two replacement domains as three independent examples, and sequence/structure benchmarks should control their overlapping provenance to avoid redundancy or train-test leakage.\",\"evidence_used\":[\"/api/v1/\",\"/api/v1/releases/1.75/pdb/1acc\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1acc\",\"/api/v1/releases/1.75/pdb/1acc/domains\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1acc/domains\",\"/api/v1/releases/1.75/sids/d1acca_\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca1\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca2\",\"/api/v1/releases/1.75/sunids/56991\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254762\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254763\",\"/api/v1/releases/1.75/sunids/56990\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254333\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254334\",\"/api/v1/releases/1.75/sunids/56989\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254146\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254147\",\"/api/v1/releases/1.75/sunids/56988\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254122\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254123\",\"/api/v1/releases/1.75/sunids/56987\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254103\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254104\",\"/api/v1/releases/1.75/sunids/56835\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/56835\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/48724\",\"/api/v1/releases\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.01/pdb/1acc/domains\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.02/pdb/1acc/domains\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.03/pdb/1acc/domains\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.04/pdb/1acc/domains\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.05/pdb/1acc/domains\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.06/pdb/1acc/domains\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.07/pdb/1acc/domains\"]}]}"}}
